:"Vila Velha is a Brazilian municipality situated on the coast of the state of Espírito Santo, in the Southeast Region of Brazil. It is part of the Greater Vitória Metropolitan Area and covers an area of 209.965 km2 (81.068 sq mi), of which 54.57 km2 (21.07 sq mi) is within the urban area. According to estimates by the Brazilian Institute of Geography and Statistics (IBGE) in 2024, its population was 502,899 inhabitants, making it the second most populous municipality in Espírito Santo, surpassed only by Serra.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Vila_Velha_ES_a_partir_do_Convento_da_Penha.JPG/330px-Vila_Velha_ES_a_partir_do_Convento_da_Penha.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vila_Velha"},"twins":["Q170322"],"climate":{"temp":[26.7,26.9,26.7,25.6,23.7,22.8,22.2,22.6,23.6,25,25.4,26.3],"rain":[140,99,138,99,76,51,47,47,50,99,200,198],"cloud":[62,56,61,56,55,49,47,47,55,67,76,72]},"land":true}